diffpdf (1:1.0.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  DiffPDF has been replaced by disparPDF, a maintained fork of it (by way
  of ConfrontaPDF), now in the package disparpdf; the diffpdf package
  only pulls that in, and can be removed.  For now "diffpdf" still runs
  disparPDF (and "man diffpdf" shows its manual page), but use
  "disparPDF" instead.

  The window, comparison modes, and -a, -c, -w and --language work as
  before.  The differences, for scripts and settings:

   - --save-and-quit[=FILE] is gone.  Use
       disparPDF --batch --pdfdiff=FILE FILE1 FILE2
     or disparPDFc, which is always in batch mode.  It prints a result
     code, which is also the exit status: 0 the same, 1 different, 2
     different numbers of pages, and others as listed by --help;
     appearance is compared unless -c or -w is given.
   - Settings are now kept in ~/.config/disparPDF/disparPDF.conf, and
     those in ~/.config/DiffPDF/ are not carried over.

 -- Barak A. Pearlmutter <bap@debian.org>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:23:50 +0100
